le 6c-11 ETF needs no exemptive order, so 485(a) applies.\n\n**Why it isn't a launch guarantee:** Effectiveness only makes the series legally registered. Launch still depends on:\n- Exchange listing approval and ticker or CUSIP assignment\n- Seed capital and authorized participant agreements\n- Custody, transfer agent, and fund accounting setup\n- Blue-sky notice filings and NSCC/DTC readiness\n- Staff comments that may require a further amendment, which can push the date back\n\n**Initial registration of a new trust:** A brand-new trust files a Form N-1A registration statement under Section 8(a) and Rule 485(a) and typically also faces the 75-day period. The trust must first be formed under state law and register under the Investment Company Act, which adds steps before any series can launch.","ttft_ms":5469,"type":"result","duration_ms":7326,"uuid":"1b8c1bb4-409a-43c2-867c-eab3fdca9cd7","ttft_stream_ms":386,"time_to_request_ms":52,"first_content_frame_ms":386,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
